# Agent working state, not source. Worktrees for parallel wave tasks live under
# .claude/worktrees/, and dispatched agents write commit-message and PR-body scratch
# beside them. None of it is the repository's, and an accidental `git add -A` sweeping
# a worktree in would commit a second copy of the whole tree. The tracked parts of
# .claude/ — the committed wave recordings under .claude/workflows/ that plan §2.1
# rule 3 requires verbatim, and agent and skill definitions — stay tracked and are
# unaffected, because these entries name directories rather than .claude/ itself.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/jobs/
.claude/scratch/
.claude/pr-scratch/

# Codex desktop working state and the local proxy discovery file are machine-local.
# They may contain nested worktrees or transient connection metadata, never source.
.codex/
proxy.port

.nx/
.vitest-report.json

# Lean build output (docs/adr/0060)
formal/.lake/

# Route fixtures tests/auth.test.ts writes into the app tree for the length of its run. A killed
# run leaves them behind (the next run removes them); they must never be committed.
apps/web/app/api/w1cp06-unregistered/
apps/web/app/p/w1cp06-unauthenticated/

# Playwright output; a run with CI set writes its HTML and JSON reports into the repository root.
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
